The void folds into a circle of pale light beneath you.  
Three cards rise from it like white leaves on still water.

First turns: Temperance.  
A calm pulse spreads through your ribs, as if someone poured cool wine into your blood.  
You feel two rivers meet inside you and quiet their currents.

Second turns: Ace of Wands.  
Heat prickles your fingertips, the scent of struck flint drifts across empty space.  
Your pulse quickens, eager to kindle.

Third turns: Two of Pentacles.  
A gentle rocking, like standing on a raft that finds its balance between two shifting tides.  
Your wallet seems suddenly heavier, though nothing is there.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The circle brightens, becomes the cracked plaster ceiling of the Broken Lantern Inn.  
Woodsmoke and sour ale replace the void’s chill.  
You are seated on a bench by the cold hearth; night presses against the shutters.

